<section class="card">
  <h2 class="card-title">Home Assistant setup</h2>
  <p class="card-subtitle mb-4">
    Import entity naming and inbound webhook recipes into Home Assistant — or paste the blueprint URL below.
  </p>
  <ul class="text-sm space-y-2 mb-4">
    <li>
      <a class="text-link" href="/ha/garage_temp_entities.yaml" download>
        Download entity naming YAML
      </a>
    </li>
    <li>
      <a class="text-link" href="/ha/garage_temp_webhook.yaml" download>
        Download webhook automation YAML
      </a>
    </li>
    <li>
      Blueprint-style import: copy
      <code class="text-xs break-all">{Astro.url.origin}/ha/garage_temp_webhook.yaml</code>
      into HA → Settings → Automations → Create → Import from YAML.
    </li>
    <li>
      Create an inbound webhook under Share, then POST <code>{"{\"action\":\"status\"}"}</code> from a rest_command.
    </li>
    <li>
      Scrape Prometheus metrics at <code>/api/v1/metrics</code> with a Pro API key.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p class="mb-0 text-sm text-[var(--color-text-muted)]">
    See also <a class="text-link" href="/docs/api">API docs</a> and the Grafana wizard on this page.
  </p>
</section>
